{"title":"Career Roadmap · Railway Engineer (IRSE/IRSME Track)","role":"Railway Engineer (IRSE/IRSME Track)","summary":"A Railway Engineer works on the planning, design, construction, maintenance, modernization, safety and operation of railway infrastructure and rolling stock systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Railway Engineering / Rail Transportation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Railway Engineer works on the planning, design, construction, maintenance, modernization, safety and operation of railway infrastructure and rolling stock systems."},{"type":"p","text":"For the IRSE/IRSME track, the engineering pathway broadly aligns with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IRSE — Indian Railway Service of Engineers, traditionally associated with Civil Engineering and railway infrastructure."},{"text":"IRSME — Indian Railway Service of Mechanical Engineers, traditionally associated with Mechanical Engineering and rolling-stock/mechanical systems."}]},{"type":"note","label":"A critical distinction","text":"IRSE/IRSME are government service cadres/recruitment pathways, not simply job titles obtained by completing a Railway Engineering specialization. Eligibility, recruitment mechanism, branch requirements and service allocation depend on the applicable UPSC/Indian Railways rules and the recruitment notification for that year."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Railway Engineering","Civil/Mechanical Engineering Fundamentals","Rail Systems","Track/Rolling Stock","Signalling & Electrification Awareness","Safety","Project Management","Data/Automation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Railway / Civil / Mechanical Engineering Fundamentals","Track / Structures / Rolling Stock / Railway Systems","Railwa